  "repair_strategy": "Add a case for keyCode 9 in _onKeyChange that calls self.hide() to close the picker immediately, then allows the browser's default Tab behavior to move focus to the next field. This ensures the picker is hidden before the blur handler runs, preventing any interference.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "pikaday.js",
      "sha256": "a50b66482ec18884a7200882e9b523d9192b224b40b296cdd4080530f114fa75",
      "before": "                switch(e.keyCode){
                    case 13:
                    case 27:
                        if (opts.field) {
                            opts.field.blur();
                        }
                        break;
                    case 37:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 1);
                        break;
                    case 38:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 7);
                        break;
                    case 39:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 1);
                        break;
                    case 40:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 7);
                        break;
                    case 8:
                    case 46:
                        self.setDate(null);
                        break;
                }",
      "after": "                switch(e.keyCode){
                    case 9:
                        // Tab key: close the picker and allow default focus movement
                        self.hide();
                        break;
                    case 13:
                    case 27:
                        if (opts.field) {
                            opts.field.blur();
                        }
                        break;
                    case 37:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 1);
                        break;
                    case 38:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 7);
                        break;
                    case 39:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 1);
                        break;
                    case 40:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 7);
                        break;
                    case 8:
                    case 46:
                        self.setDate(null);
                        break;
                }"
    }
  ],
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Pressing Tab after entering a date in the check-in field will close the datepicker and move focus to the next focusable element (the guests field), allowing keyboard-only users to continue filling the form without interruption.",
  "functional_risks": [
    "Calling hide() on Tab keydown may close the picker slightly earlier than the blur handler would, but this is consistent with user expectation that Tab moves to the next field.",
    "If the picker is not visible, the Tab case is not triggered (since it's inside the isVisible() check), so no risk there."
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
    "After typing a valid date in the check-in field and pressing Tab, the active element must be the guests input.",
    "Arrow keys (←, ↑, →, ↓) must still adjust the date when the picker is open.",
    "Enter and Escape keys must still blur the field when the picker is open.",
    "The picker should still hide appropriately when clicking outside or selecting a date."
  ]
}

